DAVID ROBERTSON (eleeakk@rosie.uh.edu) wrote:
: This happened to me when I was polymorphed into a Vampire Lord and
: a nurse started "helping" me.  I wonder if there is some type of maximum
: hitpoints for monsters?  What would happen if you drank a lot of blessed
: potions of extra healing while polymorphed?

 Minor Spoilers
You get extra hit points for the monster.  I used this technique to build
a better polyporphed monster:

A Marilith is a very good demon to become because it hits multiple
times and it has a naturally low armor class.  So even though you can't
wear armor or a cloak, your AC is still pretty low.  Unfortunately its
HP are very low.  So against a powerful opponent, they return you to
human form very quickly.  Also you wouldn't have your armor or cloak
on.  So I added to my HP.  I drank several blessed potions of extra
healing to up my HP.  I then went against the quest monster of the
wizard (I forget his name).  In one round I reduced him to 8 hitpoints,
because I hit him multiple times with MagicBane.

